    {
      "lessonNumber": 18,
      "sourceTermFace": {
        "japanese": "ひるごはん",
        "english": "lunch"
      },
      "entryKind": "lesson-sense-context-link",
      "contextualGlossEnglish": "lunch, the meal named as the object of the past eating action",
      "explanationJapanese": "「ひるごはん」は、ひるの しょくじを いう ことばです。ここでの「ごはん」は、こめだけでは なく、しょくじの いみです。「ひるごはんを」の「を」は、なにを たべたかを しめします。「たべました」は「たべる」の ていねいな かこの かたちです。この ぶんは、ひるの しょくじを した ことを はなしの じゅんばんに くわえます。",
      "explanationEnglish": "ひるごはん is lunch, the midday meal. ごはん here means a meal, not a claim that the food was rice. を marks lunch as the object of たべました, the polite past form of たべる. The sentence adds eating lunch to the sequence of completed outing actions.",
      "readerExample": {
        "sourceKind": "dialogue",
        "sourceTurnOneBased": 4,
        "japanese": "ひるごはんを たべました。",
        "english": "We ate lunch.",
        "selectedJapanese": null,
        "audioScript": null,
        "reviewed": false
      },
      "usageNoteEnglish": "The entry identifies the meal category and its grammatical role; the source does not specify a menu or exact clock time.",
